   ],
   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "th:UCB-BwCR",
    "number": "Theorem (th:UCB-BwCR)",
    "quote": "With probability $1-\\delta$, the regret of Algorithm \\ref{algo:UCB-BwCR} is bounded as\n\\EQ{0in}{0in}{\\areg_1(T) = O(L \\normOned \\textstyle{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\crad m}{T}} )}, \\ \\ \\areg_2(T) = O(\\normOned \\textstyle{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\crad m}{T}} )}}\nwhere $\\crad = O(\\log(\\frac{mTd}{\\delta}))$, ${\\bf 1}_d$ is the $d$ dimensional vector of all $1$'s."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper bounds the average regret in objective OPT_f - f(avg v); multiplied by T. Regret is in terms of concave objective of the average, not sum of rewards. Polynomial time via ellipsoid (Lemma ucbImplementability)."
  },
